INSTALL file for Hakone Media Player
====================================

Hakone is a fork of VLC media player. The recommended build instructions for
this tree use Meson and are in doc/BUILD-linux.md, doc/BUILD-macos.md and
doc/BUILD-win32.md.

More extensive information about building upstream VLC on *nix, Windows and
Mac OS X can be found here: http://wiki.videolan.org/Compile_VLC

People building for Windows from source MUST read doc/BUILD-win32.md.

Bootstrapping Hakone
====================

If you retrieved Hakone from the git server and do not have yet a "configure"
script, please run:

    ./bootstrap

Configuring Hakone
==================

A typical way to configure Hakone is:

   ./configure

See `./configure --help' for more information.

If you intend to debug stuff, you may want to compile with debugging
symbols:

   make distclean ; ./configure --enable-debug

We recommend using either GCC or Clang/LLVM to build Hakone. Specifically,
GCC version 5 or higher, or Clang/LLVM version 3.4 or higher are required.
Other compilers with compatible feature sets should also work.


Building Hakone
===============

Once configured, run `make' to build Hakone.


Installing and running Hakone
=============================

You can install Hakone and its plugins by typing:

   make install

But you don't need to install it if you don't want to; Hakone can be launched
from the current directory as well:

   ./hakone
